WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.868
-You were nominated for an Oscar
for "Benjamin Button."

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And that is a film --

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:04.738 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:05.472 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I did not realize this.

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:08.875
You -- you got a callback
after your first audition

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:10.643 size:81% position:41%
and you did not want
to go to the callback.

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:14.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, because by that point
in my career, I knew

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:19.019
that the audition room
is just so the casting directors

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
can save their ass,
so to speak.

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:23.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, because they have
already gone out to the stars.

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:24.190 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're just waiting
for one to bite the bait.

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:30.430
And so they do these auditions,
just in case the star doesn't --

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.831 size:84% position:42% line:92%
or whoever the list is.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
I knew I wasn't on that list.
-Yeah.

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:36.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] Because I was
in the audition room.

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:37.971 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So, I just knew --

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:40.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
I knew I'd been on a million
auditions and I was like,

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:42.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
they are going to have me
go through this,

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:46.446
pour my guts out in front
of this strange person,

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:48.415 line:92%
and leave my guts in there,

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:50.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then they're going to hire
somebody else.

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:52.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-You know, so I was done.

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:55.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, I'm having
a yard sale today.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.290 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.092 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I mean, it was Saturday!

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:01.961 size:81% position:41%
-Was this a previously
scheduled yard sale?

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes!
-Okay.

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:04.831 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Flyers had gone out.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:07.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
Champagne had been ordered.
I had --

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wait, what kind of yard sale
are you --

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:10.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, you got to
get 'em drunk, honey.

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.
-You got to get 'em drunk.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, so they walk in
and the champagne's just out.

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:17.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I pop the bottles right away,
get them nice and drunk.

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:18.378 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:20.680 size:75% position:38%
-And then, I'm like,
"Girl, take it all!"

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.248 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:23.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So in the end, though,
you did --

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:26.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
did you cancel the yard sale?
-I had to.

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:28.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-David Fincher was calling.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:29.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I went begrudgingly.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:33.460
-And I thought that it was going
to be like other -- a callback,

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:36.563
like, you know, several other
actresses that did a good job.

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:39.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I went in
and it was a ghost town.

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.667 line:92%
It was literally the audition --

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was just so I could meet
David Fincher.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:45.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-Laray Mayfield, I love you!

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:45.972 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's great.

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
-'Cause she casts
all of his films.

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:48.374 line:92%
-Now tell me how soon after that

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:50.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
did you reschedule
the yard sale?

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was like, "Y'all,
we just going to open --

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:54.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm going to open up
the doors today,

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:56.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
but just a couple
of hours later."

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:01.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I want to ask,
because we've talked before

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:04.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
about how Cookie is
a character that you play

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:08.194
that so many people fell in love
with immediately, and --

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah, of course.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.564 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:13.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you have --
a lot of fans

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
are drawn to Cookie
and inspired by Cookie.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:17.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
And not just female fans,
is that true?

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:18.738 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That is very true.

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:22.575
There's this tweet, and I wish
I had took a screenshot of it.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:26.379
This was a man, and I guess
he worked in corporate America.

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:28.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he was like,
"I wish I had the balls

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:31.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
"to kick in that door
in that boardroom meeting

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.219 line:92%
and walk in there like Cookie."

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:36.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "This is the best
tweet ever."

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:37.790 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.425
-Yeah, we could use more Cookie.
-I think so.

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:40.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All of us could use a little
more inner Cookie.

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think Cookie
lives in all of us.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:43.429 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:44.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's just that you have to
choose to tap into her.

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:47.500
-Yeah, she just is -- she's
inside of us, imprisoned.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, exactly. Exactly!
That's a good one.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:52.238 line:92%
-Thank you for having me.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's always
such a pleasure to see you.

